<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Practical 11 - CSS Styling</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #eaf2f8;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        h1 {
            color: white;
            background-color: #2c3e50;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        .container {
            background-color: white;
            padding: 20px;
            margin: 20px auto;
            max-width: 700px;
            border-radius: 10px;
        }

        p {
            color: #333333;
            font-size: 18px;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        .button {
            background-color: #27ae60;
            color: white;
            padding: 12px 20px;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 5px;
            cursor: pointer;
        }

        .button:hover {
            background-color: #1e8449;
        }

        footer {
            text-align: center;
            margin-top: 20px;
            color: #555555;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <h1>Welcome to My Webpage</h1>

    <div class="container">
        <h2>Introduction to CSS</h2>

        <p>
            CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets.
            It is used to style HTML webpages.
            CSS controls colors, fonts, spacing, borders,
            and the layout of a webpage.
        </p>

        <button class="button"
                onclick="alert('Welcome to my webpage!')">
            Click Here
        </button>
    </div>

    <footer>
        <p>Created for BWD Practical 11</p>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>
